jobs.description:
As a Key Account Manager, you will manage a portfolio of approximately 15 to 20 clients, primarily airlines and aircraft maintenance, repair and overhaul (MRO) organisations.

Your role combines strategic account management, business development, B2B negotiation and regular international client visits.

Your main responsibilities will include:

•   
Managing, retaining and developing your existing client portfolio;

•   
Overseeing key accounts and strategic client relationships;

•   
Understanding clients' commercial, technical and operational challenges and proposing suitable solutions;

•   
Preparing commercial proposals, responding to tenders and negotiating contracts;

•   
Maintaining regular face-to-face contact with clients and prospects;

•   
Developing new business opportunities;

•   
Preparing sales forecasts and budgets for each client;

•   
Monitoring profitability, volumes and sales performance;

•   
Conducting market analysis and keeping up with developments in the aerospace sector;

•   
Representing the company at industry events and client meetings.

The role involves regular travel across the EMEA region, accounting for approximately 50% of working time, generally on short trips.

This opportunity may particularly appeal to Account Managers, Key Account Managers, Sales Account Managers or Business Development Managers with proven experience in managing strategic client relationships.


•   
You ideally hold a Master's degree in Business, Management or a related field.

•   
You have at least four years of B2B sales experience in an international industrial environment. Experience in the aerospace sector is an advantage.

•   
You have an excellent command of French and English, with C1-level English required. Knowledge of another language used in the EMEA region is an advantage, particularly Arabic.

You stand out through:

•   
A strong customer focus;

•   
Solid negotiation skills;

•   
Excellent interpersonal and presentation skills;

•   
A sound understanding of financial and commercial considerations;

•   
The ability to work in international and multicultural environments;

•   
Autonomy, analytical thinking and effective prioritisation;

•   
The ability to collaborate effectively with a range of internal teams.

WHAT WE OFFER

Onze klant is gespecialiseerd in de behandeling van containers, trailers en nieuwe voertuigen. Daarnaast hebben zij een unieke expertise ontwikkeld in diverse havenactiviteiten, zowel op vlak van stockage en distributie, onderhoud en herstelling, als van ombouw van nieuwe voertuigen.

Jobomschrijving

Your role

• Deal with all aspects of border compliance & customs related activities in the Shipping & Port environment where the objectives are to ensure Compliance with applicable legislation and maximising the efficient flow of goods by resolving any issue that may occur;
• Liaise with Port and Customs authorities, including obtaining & maintaining the necessary authorisations (AEO, Bonded Warehouse, Temporary Storage, etc…);
• Centre of expertise for Customs matters for the organization serving internal & external stakeholders;
• Creating, maintaining & delivering organisation wide procedures, KPI’s and reports ;
• Continuously seeking to improve our operation & systems.

Your profile

• You are fluent in English.  Any additional language is an advantage;
• Ideally, you have relevant experience or knowledge in Shipping, Ports or Customs but more importantly a willingness to learn a large amount of complicated subject matter in a short timeframe;
• You are passionate and fast learner with a hands-on, problem solving mentality that doesn’t relent until an issue is resolved;
• You have excellent communication skills and the ability to create solid relations with both internal and external clients and partners;
• You are able to prioritise, work autonomously and always seek improvements;
• Once every 12 weeks, you provide a standby cover to ensure our operations are supported at all times (Weekend – Early evening).
• You meet the criteria for obtaining a legally required positive safety assessment for critical roles in the port.
